 "_about": {
  "mount": "How the game hangs each weapon part on the hunter, read from the executable (build_weapons.py). A part's type comes from 0x3506d8 (class, part index); each frame 0x34c5d8 picks its state, hunter bone and scale and the getter 0x3553b8 its {pos, rot} record. `sheathed` and `drawn` are the placement with no special motion playing: sheathed = player data +0x30 set (state 2); drawn = 0x350438's default, 1 (0 for the Dual Blades' second blade); shields and the Kinsect held (state 4) -- the Charge Blade shield too while drawn --, the scabbard and the arrows always resting (state 2). Bones: 12 / 8 the hands, 11 the forearm, 1 and 2 the waist and back, 0 the root (the arrows).",
  "records": "The record tables are filled at boot by the static initialiser 0xd4518c, run in an emulator (static_init.py): 0x109f6a0 states 0 / 4, 0x109f8c8 state 1, 0x109faf0 state 2, 0x109fd18 state 3, 23 types each; the bowguns use 0x109ff40 (drawn) / 0x109ff70 (rest), the second record for the Light Bowgun (0xb0925c). The shared types hold MH3U's own numbers, so the matrix convention is taken from the MH3U Armor Viewer, which ran its joint method.",
  "inferred": "mountJoint: the joint the record drives is the part's root joint, 0, and 4 for the Long Sword scabbard (its only joint) -- 4U's per-type joint table is not read; 3U's says the same.",
  "notRead": "Motion-specific placements (0x350438 switches on the motion id; the bowguns and others have per-motion records at 0xf2e8bc), any per-model rest override (3U had one), the weapons' own joint animation and part masks while drawn, the female scabbard offset (0x34cb68)."
 }
}